  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africa Policy, Trade &amp; Development Forum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall purpose of the joint regional initiative is to inform the target groups about the presence of the Netherlands Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries, Food Security and Nature (LNV) on the African continent. It will include the latest updates on policy developments, sustainable and new business opportunities, development activities, local needs and challenges.This event builds upon the successful East-South Africa Agri Forum and the 2023 seminar &quot;De tuinbouw van de toekomst in opkomende markten&quot; (&quot;The horticulture of the future in emerging markets&quot;). In this edition, the scope is broadened and includes North and West Africa.As the proposed event in prior to the LNV networking event, with an expected attendance 450 persons, of the LNV&apos;s &quot;Terugkomweek&quot;, this is an efficient way to explore and facilitate Dutch added value and link these to the local needs and niche opportunities and activities that Agricultural Councellors have identified in the respective countries (a.o. the combi-tracks).</narrative>
  </description>
